noderings:index/firewallRulesetAttachmen.description:
Attaches a firewall ruleset to a virtual machine. A VM has at most one ruleset; use one attachment per VM.

Only platforms with the <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`guestFirewall`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`GuestFirewall`" pulumi-lang-go="`guestFirewall`" pulumi-lang-python="`guest_firewall`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`guestFirewall`" pulumi-lang-java="`guestFirewall`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`guest_firewall`">`guestFirewall`</span> capability (Proxmox) support firewalls. Rule changes reach the VM within about a minute; the API does not report when they are applied.

The platform marks the VM as running when a ruleset is attached or detached. If the VM was stopped, this resource stops it again afterwards, so <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`powerState`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`PowerState`" pulumi-lang-go="`powerState`" pulumi-lang-python="`power_state`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`powerState`" pulumi-lang-java="`powerState`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`power_state`">`powerState`</span> on <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`noderings.VirtualMachine`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`noderings.VirtualMachine`" pulumi-lang-go="`VirtualMachine`" pulumi-lang-python="`VirtualMachine`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`noderings.VirtualMachine`" pulumi-lang-java="`noderings.VirtualMachine`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`noderings_virtual_machine`">`noderings.VirtualMachine`</span> does not drift.

