noderings:index/roleAssignment:RoleAssig.description:
Gives a user, group or service account its role in the organization. Each principal has exactly one direct role, so applying this resource replaces any role the principal had, and destroying it leaves the principal with no direct role. Use one assignment per principal.

## Example Usage

<!--Start PulumiCodeChooser -->
```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as noderings from "@noderings/pulumi";

const ops = new noderings.Group("ops", {name: "ops"});
const operator = noderings.getRole({
    name: "Operator",
});
// Everyone in the group gets the built-in Operator role.
const opsRoleAssignment = new noderings.RoleAssignment("ops", {
    groupId: ops.id,
    roleId: operator.then(operator => operator.id),
});
const auditor = noderings.getUsers({
    emails: ["carol@example.com"],
});
const viewer = noderings.getRole({
    name: "Viewer",
});
const auditorRoleAssignment = new noderings.RoleAssignment("auditor", {
    userId: auditor.then(auditor => auditor.ids?.[0]),
    roleId: viewer.then(viewer => viewer.id),
});
```
